Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ax637: enable WIRELESS/CFG80211 and BT/BT_LE
Without CONFIG_BT the esp-hosted module fails modpost because esp_bt.c
calls hci_alloc_dev/hci_register_dev. BT_LE covers the ESP32-C5
(BLE-only). CRYPTO_*/CRC16 come in via BT's selects.

--- a/arch/arm64/configs/ax637-tiny_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/ax637-tiny_defconfig
@@ -147,7 +151,18 @@
 CONFIG_NET_SCHED=y
 CONFIG_NET_CLS_ACT=y
 CONFIG_CAN=y
-# CONFIG_WIRELESS is not set
+CONFIG_WIRELESS=y
+CONFIG_CFG80211=y
+CONFIG_CFG80211_WEXT=y
+# Bluetooth: the esp-hosted host driver registers its own HCI device
+# (hci_alloc_dev/hci_register_dev in esp_bt.c), so modpost rejects the
+# module while CONFIG_BT is off. BT_LE covers the ESP32-C5 controller, which
+# is BLE-only; BT_BREDR is kept so a dual-mode module can be used later.
+# CRYPTO_*/CRC16 are pulled in by BT's selects.
+CONFIG_BT=y
+CONFIG_BT_BREDR=y
+CONFIG_BT_LE=y
+CONFIG_BT_DEBUGFS=y
 # CONFIG_ETHTOOL_NETLINK is not set
 CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
 CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
